WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.021 --> 00:00:14.964
That the students gathered in the schoolroom.

2
00:00:15.764 --> 00:00:17.405
They were talking about Miss Minchin.

3
00:00:18.465 --> 00:00:23.887
She had been angry ever since she returned from the house next door, but the students didn't know

4
00:00:23.947 --> 00:00:28.688
why. Ermengarde rushed into the room with a note in her hand.

5
00:00:29.712 --> 00:00:30.793
"Sara sent a note!"

6
00:00:31.393 --> 00:00:32.153
she exclaimed.

7
00:00:32.173 --> 00:00:35.235
"Her fortune has been given back to her.

8
00:00:36.175 --> 00:00:38.436
She's going to live with the gentleman next door!"

9
00:00:38.456 --> 00:00:42.858
"What? How did this happen?"

10
00:00:43.518 --> 00:00:44.839
the girls asked eagerly.

11
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.701
Everyone wanted to hear more from Ermengarde.

12
00:00:49.981 --> 00:00:52.783
Meanwhile little Lottie burst into tears.

13
00:00:53.563 --> 00:00:55.504
She wanted Sara to stay at the school!

14
00:00:57.188 --> 00:01:01.310
"Sara says there really were diamond mines," Ermengarde went on.

15
00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:06.332
"They were filled with millions of diamonds, and she owns half of them.

16
00:01:08.113 --> 00:01:11.434
She's invited me to visit her tomorrow, and I am going!"

17
00:01:12.735 --> 00:01:15.156
The girls chattered loudly about this news.

18
00:01:17.076 --> 00:01:22.179
Miss Minchin heard their noise and thought about scolding them, but she was not in the mood.

19
00:01:23.979 --> 00:01:25.260
Becky also heard them.

20
00:01:27.452 --> 00:01:29.874
She crept upstairs earlier than usual.

21
00:01:29.895 --> 00:01:35.640
"Well, that's the end of that," she said to herself.

22
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:42.266
Her eyes filled with tears as she climbed the last flight of stairs.

23
00:01:43.908 --> 00:01:48.212
She wanted to have one last look at the beautiful things in Sara's room.

24
00:01:48.232 --> 00:01:52.536
"No more fire or rosy lamp," she thought.

25
00:01:53.652 --> 00:01:57.354
"No more supper or anyone telling me stories all night long."

26
00:01:59.095 --> 00:02:01.957
She choked back a sob as she opened the door.

27
00:02:03.397 --> 00:02:05.278
But then she let out a low cry.

28
00:02:05.959 --> 00:02:09.160
A fire was blazing—and there stood Ram Dass.

29
00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:12.842
"Miss Sara did not forget you," he said.

30
00:02:12.862 --> 00:02:16.384
"Tomorrow you will go next door to live as her maid."

31
00:02:17.645 --> 00:02:21.127
"What?" Becky could not believe what she was hearing.

32
00:02:21.147 --> 00:02:24.468
"And here's some supper," said Ram Dass.

33
00:02:24.488 --> 00:02:27.109
"Oh, thank you!"

34
00:02:27.869 --> 00:02:29.110
Becky shouted happily.

35
00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.171
As time passed, Sara became very close friends with Mr.

36
00:02:34.211 --> 00:02:40.633
Carrisford. The gentleman had never had a companion whom he liked as much as he liked Sara!

37
00:02:42.314 --> 00:02:45.094
One evening they were sitting together as usual.

38
00:02:46.015 --> 00:02:47.555
Mr. Carrisford was reading.

39
00:02:48.675 --> 00:02:50.456
Sara was staring into the fire.

40
00:02:52.456 --> 00:02:53.937
"What are you thinking about, Sara?"

41
00:02:54.338 --> 00:02:54.918
he asked.

42
00:02:55.979 --> 00:02:58.421
She looked up, her cheeks bright pink.

43
00:02:58.441 --> 00:03:02.205
"I was remembering a day when I was hungry."

44
00:03:02.225 --> 00:03:06.188
"You were hungry many days," Mr.

45
00:03:06.228 --> 00:03:07.329
Carrisford replied.

46
00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:09.811
"Which hungry day was it?"

47
00:03:09.831 --> 00:03:13.895
"The day when I gave the buns to the beggar girl."

48
00:03:14.936 --> 00:03:19.380
Sara told him about finding money in the sloppy mud outside the bakery.

49
00:03:20.664 --> 00:03:22.726
"You say that I have so much money now.

50
00:03:23.606 --> 00:03:26.088
Do you think I could use some to help the poor?"

51
00:03:26.108 --> 00:03:28.510
"What would you do?"

52
00:03:29.091 --> 00:03:30.792
Mr. Carrisford asked softly.

53
00:03:32.373 --> 00:03:33.394
Sara hesitated.

54
00:03:33.414 --> 00:03:37.877
"I'd like the baker to feed any hungry children she sees.

55
00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:40.580
Then she could send the bill to me."

56
00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:43.942
Mr. Carrisford instantly nodded.

57
00:03:43.962 --> 00:03:46.004
"That's a wonderful idea!"

58
00:03:48.416 --> 00:03:50.277
The next day Sara and Mr.

59
00:03:50.297 --> 00:03:51.997
Carrisford visited the baker.

60
00:03:53.978 --> 00:03:55.738
The woman looked closely at Sara.

61
00:03:55.758 --> 00:03:58.039
"Have we met before?"

62
00:03:58.879 --> 00:04:00.219
Her friendly face lit up.

63
00:04:01.299 --> 00:04:07.161
"I feel that I remember you, but I cannot quite—" "You once gave me six buns when I

64
00:04:07.201 --> 00:04:08.661
could only pay for four!"

65
00:04:09.142 --> 00:04:09.862
said Sara.

66
00:04:09.882 --> 00:04:13.843
"And then you gave five of them to a beggar child!"

67
00:04:14.483 --> 00:04:15.363
the woman replied.

68
00:04:15.383 --> 00:04:17.864
"I always remembered that."

69
00:04:19.488 --> 00:04:20.888
The baker turned to Mr.

70
00:04:20.909 --> 00:04:24.710
Carrisford. "There aren't many children who would do that."

71
00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.771
She looked closely at Sara again.

72
00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:31.012
"Excuse me, miss, but you look different.

73
00:04:32.112 --> 00:04:35.433
Your cheeks are rosy now, and you appear quite healthy."

74
00:04:35.453 --> 00:04:39.234
"My life has changed," Sara said.

75
00:04:39.254 --> 00:04:44.596
"I was wondering if you could do something for me."

76
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:49.302
She explained her plan involving poor children and free buns.

77
00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:53.805
The woman watched her, listening with an astonished face.

78
00:04:53.825 --> 00:04:58.627
"Why, I'd be happy to do that," said the baker.

79
00:04:58.647 --> 00:05:02.049
"In fact you've already inspired me.

80
00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:07.172
You looked so cold and hungry, and yet you gave away those buns.

81
00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:10.734
I've often fed poor children since that day."

82
00:05:10.754 --> 00:05:15.516
"I wonder where that beggar girl is now," Sara said.

83
00:05:15.536 --> 00:05:18.378
"Why, she's right here!"

84
00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.158
the baker replied.

85
00:05:20.178 --> 00:05:23.800
"I told her to come back whenever she was hungry.

86
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.741
I gave her odd jobs and she turned out to be a good worker.

87
00:05:28.962 --> 00:05:30.262
Her name is Anne."

88
00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:34.244
The baker went into the back room and brought Anne out.

89
00:05:35.644 --> 00:05:37.605
Anne was healthy and well fed now.

90
00:05:38.686 --> 00:05:41.247
The two girls stood looking at each other for a minute.

91
00:05:42.347 --> 00:05:45.276
Then Sara held out her hand, and Anne took it.

92
00:05:45.296 --> 00:05:49.398
"I'm so glad that you're doing well," said Sara.

93
00:05:49.418 --> 00:05:52.719
"The baker is going to give buns to poor children.

94
00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.821
Perhaps you'd like to be the one who hands out the food.

95
00:05:57.882 --> 00:06:00.703
After all, you know what it's like to be hungry."

96
00:06:00.723 --> 00:06:04.044
"Oh yes, miss," said Anne.

97
00:06:04.064 --> 00:06:06.045
"I'd like that very much."

98
00:06:07.325 --> 00:06:09.666
The little princess was very pleased.

99
00:06:09.686 --> 00:06:14.850
"You'll quickly discover what I have discovered," she told Anne.

100
00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:18.455
"There is great joy in giving."
